    "body": "## Summary\n\nFix an existing `main` bug in the SeaweedFS L3 backend. MLA KV is replicated across TP ranks, but Mamba state is TP-sharded and `should_backup` makes every TP rank back up its own shard. `key_scope()` drops the TP rank for MLA models, so every rank writes the same `<key>.mamba` object and restores another rank's state.\n\nFollowing #43594 (the same fix for NIXL): on MLA models, Mamba component keys carry the TP rank (`<key>.mamba.tp{rank}of{size}`); KV and other pools keep their keys. Existing rank-ambiguous Mamba objects are not reused because their owning rank is unknown, so they read as misses.\n\nSplit out of #41907 so each storage backend is reviewed on its own.\n\n## Tests\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest -q test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_hicache_seaweedfs_storage.py\n```\n\n- New `test_v2_mla_mamba_state_stays_per_rank`: two MLA TP ranks write the same page keys with different Mamba payloads and must each read back their own; KV keys stay shared.\n- This PR: 15 passed, 17 subtests passed.\n- Negative control (same test against the `main` backend): the new test fails.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38231172485](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38231172485)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38231171991](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38231171991)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38231172584](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38231172584)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
